  "title": "scorecard --economy: skill_scorecard.economy tolerates a None skills_used context",
  "spec": "Goal T-1403, wave 2, plan label E11 (part a).\n\nReproduced 2026-10-01: `uv run orchestrator scorecard --economy` in /Users/k3ntaw/code/orchestrator raises\n  File \"orchestrator/skill_scorecard.py\", line 493, in economy\n    skills = sorted({s for r in rows for s in (r.get(\"context\") or {}).get(\"skills_used\", [])})\n  TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not iterable\n(called from build() at skill_scorecard.py:439). bus.log_run writes context keys with value None\n(orchestrator/bus.py ~340-347), so .get('skills_used', []) returns None.\n\nChange: skill_scorecard.py:493 uses `... .get(\"skills_used\") or []`. Check the rest of economy() (476-499) and\nbuild() for the same .get(key, default) pattern on context keys that can be None, and apply `or []`/`or 0` there\ntoo. Lines 481-483 and 396/419 already use `or []`.\n\nTests: add test_economy_tolerates_none_skills_used beside test_economy_reuse_requires_all_selected_used (~219) in\ntests/test_skill_scorecard.py. No existing test pins the failing behaviour. After the fix,\n`uv run orchestrator scorecard --economy` must print instead of raising (state it in the result; do not commit any\nscorecard output).\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused tests in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate. Write tests as unittest.TestCase methods using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
